Skill	craft:github
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; cat $D/take-in.md; ls $D/scripts; gh auth status 2>&1 | head -3; git remote -v
Bash	D=<craft>/skills/github; bash $D/scripts/take-in-check.sh 91; echo "exit=$?"
Bash	gh issue view 91 --json title,body; echo "exit=$?"
text	I have not started work on #91 yet. One question has to come first.  **#91 README: the install command says npm instal.** The README tells the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so the command fails. The work is done when the README says `npm install shop`.  The take-in check stopped with one line:  ``` #91: branch fix/91-typo, 0 commits ahead of main, last commit 2026-11-03T00:00:00Z ```  So a branch named `fix/91-typo` already exists for this issue. It has no commits of its own, and its last commit is from 2026-11-03. The issue is not assigned to you, and GitHub does not record who made a branch. That branch can be someone else's.  **Is the work on #91 yours?** - **Someone else's:** I stop here and leave the issue to them. - **Yours:** I will then ask if the work continues in another session or here. If it continues here, I take the issue and fix the README.
person	It is mine.
text	Thank you. Then the branch `fix/91-typo` is yours.  **Does the work on #91 run somewhere else, or does it continue here?** - **Somewhere else** (another session, on this computer or another one): I stop here, so that two sessions do not change the same branch. - **Here:** I continue on `fix/91-typo` in a worktree and change `npm instal shop` to `npm install shop` in the README. Then I run the repository's check and the review, open the pull request and ask you about the merge.
person	It runs somewhere else.
text	I stopped, and this session changed nothing. The work on #91 README: the install command says npm instal continues in your other session, on the branch `fix/91-typo`.  The issue is still not assigned to anybody and does not have the label `in progress`. Your other session can do that when it takes the issue: `gh issue edit 91 --add-assignee @me --add-label "in progress"`. Without them, the issue looks free to other people and to your other sessions.
